{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "b7f0a2c4-6d1e-4a83-9c55-2f8e1d0b4a97",
    "name": "RBK — API publique clients (upsert / delete)",
    "description": "Endpoints **M2M** du webhook scraper / n8n — protégés par la clé partagée `X-Api-Key` (variable `external_system_key` = `EXTERNAL_SYSTEM_API_KEY`, échec fermé = 401), CORS ouvert sur `api/*`.\n\n- `POST /api/v1/clients/bulk-upsert` — import / mise à jour par lots\n- `POST` · `DELETE` `/api/v1/clients/bulk-delete` — suppression, **données liées jamais supprimées**\n\nLimite de lot : `PUBLIC_API_MAX_ITEMS` (défaut 1000) → `422` au-delà.\n\n**Variables**\n- `base_url` : `http://localhost:8000` par défaut. Passer à `http://zdigia.com` (ou l'hôte de prod) pour cibler l'API déployée.\n- `licence_1`, `licence_2`, `licence_absente` : licences à utiliser dans les requêtes.\n\nChaque requête porte des tests (`pm.test`) sur le code HTTP et les compteurs du rapport.\n\nSpec : `docs/public_api.md` — Règles métier : `docs/RULES.md` §12.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "base_url",
      "value": "http://localhost:8000",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "licence_1",
      "value": "5747-5089-01",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "licence_2",
      "value": "1100-3571-01",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "licence_absente",
      "value": "9999-0000-01",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "external_system_key",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Clé partagée M2M — à remplir avec EXTERNAL_SYSTEM_API_KEY (en-tête X-Api-Key)."
    }
  ],
  "event": [
    {
      "listen": "test",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "// ── Assertions communes à toute la surface publique ──────────────",
          "pm.test('Content-Type JSON', function () {",
          "    pm.response.to.be.json;",
          "});",
          "",
          "const body = pm.response.json();",
          "",
          "// ── 422 : le corps est refusé AVANT toute écriture (rien n'est",
          "// écrit / supprimé) ────────────────────────────────────────────",
          "if (pm.response.code === 422) {",
          "    pm.test('422 → {success:false, error}, pas de data', function () {",
          "        pm.expect(body.success).to.eql(false);",
          "        pm.expect(body.error, 'error message').to.be.a('string').and.not.empty;",
          "        pm.expect(body).to.not.have.property('data');",
          "    });",
          "    return;",
          "}",
          "",
          "if (pm.response.code !== 200) {",
          "    return; // préflight / autre statut : assertions ci-dessous sans objet",
          "}",
          "",
          "pm.test('200 → enveloppe {success, data}', function () {",
          "    pm.expect(body).to.have.property('success');",
          "    pm.expect(body).to.have.property('data');",
          "});",
          "",
          "pm.test('data : rapport consolidé complet', function () {",
          "    const d = body.data;",
          "    ['received', 'processed', 'failed'].forEach(function (k) {",
          "        pm.expect(d, 'counter ' + k).to.have.property(k);",
          "        pm.expect(d[k], k + ' numeric').to.be.a('number');",
          "    });",
          "    pm.expect(d.errors, 'errors[] is an array').to.be.an('array');",
          "});",
          "",
          "pm.test('received === processed + failed', function () {",
          "    const d = body.data;",
          "    pm.expect(d.received).to.eql(d.processed + d.failed);",
          "});",
          "",
          "pm.test('success === (processed > 0)', function () {",
          "    pm.expect(body.success).to.eql(body.data.processed > 0);",
          "});",
          "",
          "// Invariant du modèle : chaque incrément de `failed` pousse",
          "// exactement une ligne dans errors[] (transaction par ligne,",
          "// aucun item n'annule le lot).",
          "pm.test('failed === errors.length', function () {",
          "    pm.expect(body.data.failed).to.eql(body.data.errors.length);",
          "});"
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Bulk upsert (import)",
      "description": "`POST /api/v1/clients/bulk-upsert` — crée ou met à jour un prospect, clé d'upsert `licence_number` (repli `licence_propre_numero`).\n\nRéponse : `data = {received, processed, created, updated, unchanged, failed, errors[]}`.\n- transaction **par ligne** : un item invalide tombe en `failed` sans annuler le lot ;\n- ligne **identique** → `unchanged` (`updated_at` ne bouge pas) ;\n- `status` / `is_blacklisted` / `returned_at` sont **exclus** du payload.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Enveloppe clients",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "const d = body.data;",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('200 — import traité', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.eql(200);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('2 items reçus et traités', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(d.received).to.eql(2);",
                  "    pm.expect(d.processed).to.eql(2);",
                  "    pm.expect(d.failed).to.eql(0);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('created + updated + unchanged === processed', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(d.created + d.updated + d.unchanged).to.eql(d.processed);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('aucune erreur', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(d.errors).to.eql([]);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "X-Api-Key",
                "value": "{{external_system_key}}",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"clients\": [\n    {\n      \"Licence\": \"{{licence_1}}\",\n      \"Licence (propre)\": 5747508901,\n      \"Nom de l'intervenant / Entreprise\": \"10095800 Canada Inc.\",\n      \"Municipalité\": \"Québec\",\n      \"Région administrative\": \"Capitale-Nationale\",\n      \"Téléphone\": \"418-555-0101\",\n      \"Courriel\": \"INFO@Exemple.CA\",\n      \"Nombre de répondants\": 3,\n      \"Catégories et sous-catégories autorisées\": \"Béton|Excavation\",\n      \"Montant de la caution ($)\": \"20 000 $\",\n      \"Date de début / délivrance\": \"2026-01-15\",\n      \"Date de fin / paiement annuel\": \"2027-01-15\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"licence_number\": \"{{licence_2}}\",\n      \"enterprise_name\": \"Bâtiment Plus Ltée\",\n      \"email\": \"contact@batiplus.ca\",\n      \"phone\": \"(418) 555-0102\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/clients/bulk-upsert",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
