    {
      "name": "Bulk delete (suppression)",
      "description": "`POST` · `DELETE` `/api/v1/clients/bulk-delete` — les deux verbes pointent sur la **même action**.\n\nRéponse : `data = {received, processed, deleted, skipped, missing, failed, skipped_items[], missing_items[], errors[]}`.\n\n**Garde-fou** : `reservations`, `notes` et `rappels` sont tous `cascadeOnDelete()`. Un client qui en porte est **`skipped`** (avec le compte par table) et la boucle passe au suivant — son historique n'est jamais détruit. Licence inexistante → `missing` (**pas** une erreur).",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Enveloppe licences (POST)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const d = pm.response.json().data;",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('200 — lot examiné', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.eql(200);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('3 items reçus et traités', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(d.received).to.eql(3);",
                  "    pm.expect(d.processed).to.eql(3);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('deleted + skipped + missing === processed', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(d.deleted + d.skipped + d.missing).to.eql(d.processed);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('licence absente → missing (pas une erreur)', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(d.missing).to.be.at.least(1);",
                  "    pm.expect(d.missing_items).to.be.an('array').that.is.not.empty;",
                  "    pm.expect(d.missing_items[0]).to.have.property('licence_number');",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test('chaque skipped_item expose ses liens', function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(d.skipped_items).to.be.an('array');",
                  "    d.skipped_items.forEach(function (s) {",
                  "        pm.expect(s.linked, 'linked').to.be.an('object');",
                  "        ['reservations', 'notes', 'rappels'].forEach(function (t) {",
                  "            pm.expect(s.linked[t], 'linked.' + t).to.be.a('number');",
                  "        });",
                  "    });",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Accept",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "X-Api-Key",
                "value": "{{external_system_key}}",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"licences\": [\"{{licence_1}}\", \"{{licence_2}}\", \"{{licence_absente}}\"]\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/clients/bulk-delete",
              "host": [
                "{{base_url}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "clients",
                "bulk-delete"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Le 3e item est volontairement absent → `missing`.\n\nÀ tester dans l'ordre : importer d'abord (dossier ci-dessus), puis supprimer — un client tout juste importé est *vierge* et sera réellement `deleted`."
          }
        },
